Week 2 — Business Intelligence & Power BI Dashboard

Project Overview

This project analyzes the Superstore retail dataset using Microsoft Power BI to evaluate sales performance, profitability, customer segments, regional performance, and product performance between 2014 and 2017.

Tools Used

- Microsoft Power BI
- Power Query
- DAX
- GitHub

Dashboard

The Power BI dashboard contains two analytical pages:

Page 1 — Overall Sales Performance

- KPI cards
- Sales and profit trend
- Sales by region
- Profit by region
- Sales by customer segment
- Sales by state
- Interactive Year and Category slicers

Page 2 — Product Performance & Profitability

- Profit by product
- Profit by subcategory
- Sales and profit by category
- Product profitability table
- Interactive filters

Key KPIs

Metric | Result 

Total Sales | $2.0M 
Total Profit | $286K 
Total Orders | ~5K 
Average Sales | $230 
Profit Margin | 12.5% 

Key Insights

1. Sales increased significantly between 2014 and 2017.
2. Sales generally strengthened between August and December.
3. The West region was consistently one of the strongest-performing regions.
4. Technology was the most consistently strong category.
5. Tables and Bookcases presented profitability concerns due to recurring negative margins.

Recommendations

- Review the profitability of Tables and Bookcases.
- Diversify regional revenue.
- Protect high-performing markets while expanding weaker regions.
- Optimize inventory and marketing around seasonal demand.
- Prioritize consistently profitable products.
- Evaluate discounts based on both sales performance and profitability.

Deliverables

- Business Intelligence Overview Report
- Executive Summary Report
- Dashboard Export
